1
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:04,440
Shima-san, are you okay?

2
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,960
I believe I told you, Young Su,

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:14,070
that our bodies constantly deplete,
 like a spirit's.

4
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:17,760
I know there are three of 
you Ryuzus that alternate,

5
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:21,640
but since you were removed from 
the rotation, there's no replacement.

6
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:27,790
I cannot say for certain that I will 
last until Emilia-sama returns.

7
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:31,400
So I will say what must be said.

8
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,890
You don't hafta push yourself like that!

9
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:35,750
The healthy old hag right 
here can take your—

10
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:39,610
That's too confusing! 
Call them Old Shi and Old Ryu!

11
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:41,620
Besides, that won't work.

12
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:45,270
Only Shima-san can tell us this.

13
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:53,200
Yes, only I, one who has entered the graveyard
 and attempted the trial, can speak of it.

14
00:00:55,170 --> 00:00:58,410
It is about the memories of Ryuzu Meyer,

15
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:03,180
the progenitor we copies are derived from.

16
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:14,100
It happened before this place 
became known as the Sanctuary.

17
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:26,690
The beginning of this unknown memory

18
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:29,680
was a young girl with a lovely face,

19
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:35,890
skin as white as snow, and pale blue eyes.

20
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:40,320
What is it, I suppose?

21
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:42,800
Look at me that way all you want,

22
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,450
but I won't give you anything.

23
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,960
Hmph. Silent again.

24
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:55,900
What a boring, cowardly girl you are, I suppose.

25
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:01,100
Beatrice, why the attitude?

26
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,380
Echidna-sama...

27
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:08,050
Did I teach you to behave that way?

28
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:10,780
Uh... Y-You're mistaken, Mother!

29
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,410
I didn't do anything!

30
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:13,650
It's just...

31
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,430
This girl was...

32
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,600
I see.

33
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:21,200
Then why don't we hear what she has to say?

34
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:24,740
Wha... um... well...

35
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:29,000
Yes. I'm very sorry.

36
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,730
I saw her standing there, 
looking so wistful,

37
00:02:31,730 --> 00:02:33,880
and I was captivated.

38
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,180
Captivated, eh?

39
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:41,340
Beatrice, you heard Ryuzu.

40
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:44,160
Mew...

41
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:50,570
It would be inaccurate to call you childish,
 since you <i>are</i> a child,

42
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:52,900
but your attitude lacks tolerance.

43
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,720
It's true that you are special,

44
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,400
but not so that you can look down on others.

45
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,780
I'm sorry to startle you.

46
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,520
This is Beatrice.

47
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,840
She is like a daughter to me.

48
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,280
I'm not "like" your daughter!

49
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,950
I <i>am</i> your daughter, I suppose!

50
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,840
Yes, well, there you have it.

51
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:18,420
I believe she'll be accompanying 
me here often from now on.

52
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:20,300
Please do be kind to her.

53
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:24,470
Y-Yes, you can count on me, Echidna-sama.

54
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:25,470
I don't need her.

55
00:03:25,790 --> 00:03:29,140
I'm just fine on my own.

56
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:33,760
That was how the two girls met.

57
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:41,050
After that, the witch and her daughter 
visited the settlement occasionally.

58
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:46,830
Why are you just standing there, I suppose?

59
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:50,180
I see you're as dull as ever.

60
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,760
Beatrice-sama...

61
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:54,370
Mother is having a discussion inside.

62
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,000
She'll be back when she finishes,

63
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,600
so hurry up and put that irritating 
laundry in the basket, I suppose.

64
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,820
O-Of course.

65
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,390
Excuse me.

66
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:20,280
Um, Beatrice-sama?

67
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:23,490
It's nothing. Just killing time, I suppose.

68
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:35,020
Beatrice-sama...

69
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,550
U-Um, if you don't mind,

70
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:42,910
would you help me fold the laundry?

71
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:44,760
What?!

72
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:51,440
If it's too much for you to handle alone,

73
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:54,060
I suppose I have no choice but to help you.

74
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:56,520
Huh?

75
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,310
I won't say it again, I suppose!

76
00:04:58,310 --> 00:05:00,860
Well, get going, then! Let's go, I suppose!

77
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:12,600
U-Um, if you don't mind, would 
you carry a little bit of it?

78
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,840
Listen...

79
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,250
Don't go pushing your luck.

80
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:19,500
Just this much, I suppose.

81
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:24,840
So when the witch had 
business to attend to,

82
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:29,970
the young girl would spend 
her time with Ryuzu Meyer.

83
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:35,060
You, there. Pardon me.

84
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:38,240
I believe Echidna-sama is here.

85
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,370
Have you seen her?

86
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,670
What?

87
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,230
M-Mathers-sama!

88
00:05:44,950 --> 00:05:48,320
I'm not fond of being addressed 
by my family name.

89
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:52,410
Would you just call me Roswaal?

90
00:05:52,410 --> 00:05:53,830
Hang on a minute!

91
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:57,490
Beatrice was in the Sanctuary? 
And Roswaal, too?

92
00:05:57,490 --> 00:06:00,790
More accurately, that was the Roswaal-sama 
of several generations ago.

93
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:04,250
But it sounds as if Beatrice-sama 
hasn't changed.

94
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:07,730
I'm more interested in the witch.

95
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:11,530
I know this is the Witch of 
Greed's experimental facility,

96
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:14,840
but I've never actually heard her story.

97
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:18,820
Really? You never met the 
witch in the trials?

98
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:21,650
I only went in to settle a score.

99
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:23,410
I didn't meet the witch.

100
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:26,130
But when you say that, it sounds like you...

101
00:06:26,130 --> 00:06:29,340
Have you met the Witch of Greed, Barusu?

102
00:06:30,770 --> 00:06:31,490
Yeah.

103
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:33,360
I see.

104
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:37,010
To one who was not alive during that time,

105
00:06:37,010 --> 00:06:41,040
the witch may indeed seem 
quite out of reach.

106
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,800
Of course, even my memories 
are those of another.

107
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,600
I do not know her personally.

108
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,790
Seeing one who looks identical 
to me saying that

109
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:53,550
makes me feel as if I've 
gone mad. How frightening.

110
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:55,720
I feel like I'm listening to clones 
telling dark jokes.

111
00:06:55,970 --> 00:07:01,990
Beatrice-sama is an exceedingly common 
presence in Ryuzu Meyer's memories.

112
00:07:01,990 --> 00:07:05,730
They had quite the heartwarming friendship.

113
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,800
Go ahead and finish the story.

114
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,800
The Sanctuary seemed so 
peaceful on the surface,

115
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,060
so what happened?

116
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,660
It collapsed.

117
00:07:18,050 --> 00:07:23,920
Then the true reason for the 
Sanctuary's existence came along.

118
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,940
The true reason... for its existence?

119
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:42,140
Sin Archbishop of the Witch's Cult,
representing Greed...

120
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:44,760
Regulus Corneas.

121
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:47,740
A Sin Archbishop of the Witch's Cult?

122
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:49,650
What are you doing here?

123
00:07:49,910 --> 00:07:54,840
I was assured that no one could get 
involved with this forest except me!

124
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:57,010
Assured?

125
00:07:57,010 --> 00:08:00,920
I think you just made up that 
rule and assured yourself.

126
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:04,640
And now you're trying to force 
other people to go along with it?

127
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:07,570
Pretty cocky for some worthless spirit.

128
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,970
If you dislike the rule,

129
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:12,410
then talk it over with the church!

130
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:14,340
Why have you come here?!

131
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:16,090
Because...

132
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:19,060
I ordered him to.

133
00:08:31,150 --> 00:08:34,910
What's the matter, Bishop Romanée-Conti?

134
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:36,910
Why...

135
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,960
Why are you here?!

136
00:08:39,490 --> 00:08:42,970
Regulus Corneas! Why is she here?!

137
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:46,720
Hah! She came here of her own will.

138
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,830
Why are you blaming everything on me?

139
00:08:48,830 --> 00:08:50,830
You got something against me?

140
00:08:50,830 --> 00:08:55,670
Bishop Corneas, he is simply confused.

141
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:57,900
Try not to criticize him so much.

142
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:04,700
Now, bring the key and seal here,

143
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:07,940
so that the Witch's Cult can fulfill 
its long-cherished desire.

144
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:09,770
Pandora!

145
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,650
Oh?

146
00:09:13,650 --> 00:09:15,380
Enjoy being skewered!

147
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:18,070
And apologize to my brother and his wife!

148
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:22,370
Now begone forever!

149
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:31,540
Hey, come on.

150
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:35,050
You weren't even aiming anywhere near me,

151
00:09:35,050 --> 00:09:38,260
but you used an attack that 
you knew would hit me, too?

152
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:40,760
That's the same as trampling on my life,

153
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:46,850
on my existence, on my authority, 
on my humanity itself, isn't it?

154
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,260
Fortuna-sama!

155
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:03,990
Please take Emilia-sama and leave here.

156
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:06,010
Mother...

157
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:07,850
Emilia...

158
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,710
Worry not.

159
00:10:10,330 --> 00:10:14,170
I would not remain here without a plan.

160
00:10:18,250 --> 00:10:20,610
I swear I'll come back to help you!

161
00:10:20,610 --> 00:10:21,510
I swear it!

162
00:10:21,510 --> 00:10:22,880
Geuse!

163
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:27,060
Keeping the trial in mind, 
you should be following yourself, no?

164
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:28,160
What will you do?

165
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:31,230
Hey, that was pretty admirable.

166
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:35,570
But who gave you permission 
to let them get away?

167
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:40,250
That's a violation of my actions 
and authority, isn't it?

168
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:41,940
Say what you will.

169
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,120
If it means risking my very existence,

170
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:47,410
I cannot allow the two of 
you to get past this point!

171
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,570
Wait, you're not gonna...

172
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:57,300
I do not have the knowledge 
to adapt to this.

173
00:10:57,650 --> 00:11:01,650
For that reason, I have done nothing but 
hold it since I was entrusted with it.

174
00:11:01,650 --> 00:11:04,830
But it was meant for a moment such as this!

175
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:09,090
Bishop Petelgeuse Romanée-Conti...

176
00:11:11,010 --> 00:11:12,440
Have a good journey.

177
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,530
Please... forgive me...

178
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,290
Flugel-sama!

179
00:11:40,230 --> 00:11:41,450
What an idiot.

180
00:11:46,730 --> 00:11:48,680
Magnificent...

181
00:11:51,530 --> 00:11:53,650
Bishop Regulus Corneas.

182
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:55,860
Yes?

183
00:11:57,170 --> 00:11:58,360
Here it comes.

184
00:12:13,170 --> 00:12:15,380
I told you...

185
00:12:15,930 --> 00:12:19,240
What you see here is hope.

186
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:24,910
A great, unforgettable debt to the 
people who made me what I am.

187
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,600
So now...

188
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:31,320
If I am worthy of spitting up blood...

189
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:36,100
What do you see with those crimson eyes,

190
00:12:36,710 --> 00:12:38,400
Bishop Romanée-Conti?

191
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,570
Love.

192
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:43,280
I will not let you pursue those two.

193
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:49,980
I will not allow you to get past me!

194
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:56,670
Geuse, what... What did you do?!

195
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:59,630
A splendid show of your resolve,

196
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:02,230
Bishop Petelgeuse Romanée-Conti.

197
00:13:02,730 --> 00:13:05,280
In the name of the Witch of Vanity,

198
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:08,000
for your resolve and steadfast will,

199
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,220
I grant you the title of Sloth.

200
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:14,850
Do you think I desire such a title?

201
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:17,230
There is only one thing I desire right now:

202
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:20,980
peace for that mother and her child!

203
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,650
Love...

204
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,360
How wonderful.

205
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,840
This lie you utter...

206
00:13:28,750 --> 00:13:32,790
is a warmth that can never come to pass!

207
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,000
Hey, listen...

208
00:13:42,130 --> 00:13:44,690
I showed up here, I'm standing here,

209
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:47,010
and you're just gonna ignore me?

210
00:13:47,010 --> 00:13:49,130
What are you thinking?

211
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:49,800
No...

212
00:13:50,610 --> 00:13:52,900
Regulus Corneas!

213
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:54,770
It pisses me off!

214
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:58,190
There's no way you should be 
chosen by the Witch Factor,

215
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:01,760
but you're holding on to it with no 
regard for the payment it requires?

216
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,430
I don't care what you say! I will—

217
00:14:16,650 --> 00:14:17,910
A repetition draw.

218
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,960
While they're locked in a stalemate,

219
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,640
something should be happening 
with the other two.

220
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:25,710
You're saying we should leave here?

221
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:28,270
But look at what Geuse is 
putting himself through!

222
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:32,970
It's debatable whether or not the strength 
of one's will could have affected the outcome.

223
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:35,680
Then can't we just stand here and watch?

224
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,560
I want to—

225
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:48,950
It looks like even your insufficient brain 
has realized which is the wiser choice.

226
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:56,050
Change of location.

227
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:59,460
We're moving to where you 
and your mother fled.

228
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:03,680
No! No, Mother!

229
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:06,000
Please, Emilia. I'll be 
right back, so just...

230
00:15:04,850 --> 00:15:07,490
No! You can't!

231
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:10,410
You have the same look on 
your face that Geuse did!

232
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:13,260
Don't leave me! Don't leave me behind!

233
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:16,540
I won't lie or break my promises anymore!

234
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:20,140
I'll be good! I'll be a good girl!

235
00:15:21,570 --> 00:15:22,550
Emilia...

236
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,110
Emilia... Emilia...

237
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:27,880
Emilia...

238
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:36,530
Mother Fortuna...

239
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:46,670
Mother Fortuna... was my real mother.

240
00:15:50,540 --> 00:15:52,080
Mother Fortuna...

241
00:15:52,830 --> 00:15:53,860
I love you.

242
00:15:55,410 --> 00:15:56,260
Fortuna-sama!

243
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:04,100
Archi, are the villagers safe?

244
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,640
The news is not good.

245
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:12,190
The men are fighting the people 
who arrived with the bishop.

246
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:15,230
If we stay in the forest, 
we'll be found eventually.

247
00:16:15,230 --> 00:16:16,620
They're after...

248
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:19,470
The seal, right?

249
00:16:19,850 --> 00:16:21,540
How did they find out about it?

250
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,740
Even that woman...

251
00:16:27,330 --> 00:16:29,290
Fine. I'll be right there.

252
00:16:29,290 --> 00:16:31,820
No, we will fight.

253
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,970
You must take Emilia 
and leave the forest!

254
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:35,840
And what happens if I run away now?!

255
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,380
If they get their hands on the seal,

256
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:40,400
the world <i>will</i> end this time!

257
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:46,950
I'm sorry you had to go through 
all this to protect us.

258
00:16:46,950 --> 00:16:48,480
Please don't say that!

259
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:51,120
Who would show such disdain 
for a family member?!

260
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:52,670
I'm sorry.

261
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:56,070
Emilia...

262
00:16:56,480 --> 00:17:01,550
I have to go and fulfill a very 
important duty to protect everyone.

263
00:17:02,010 --> 00:17:04,560
So I have to leave for a 
little while, all right?

264
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:07,890
No, Mother! I... I...

265
00:17:07,890 --> 00:17:10,660
Please do as I say.

266
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:13,550
I want you to leave this forest with Archi.

267
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:21,970
Fortuna-sama... I—

268
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:22,850
Archi...

269
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:25,540
It's a bit early,

270
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:27,920
but I'm entrusting you with the 
mission of the forest dwellers.

271
00:17:28,590 --> 00:17:30,540
Please take Emilia away from here.

272
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:33,110
This world isn't easy to live in,

273
00:17:33,110 --> 00:17:34,640
but I know there's hope.

274
00:17:35,610 --> 00:17:37,030
I'm sure of it.

275
00:17:37,030 --> 00:17:39,560
I can't! I must stay with everyone until—

276
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,540
Take Emilia.

277
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:41,890
Please.

278
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:47,740
She's the beloved daughter of 
my brother, his wife, and myself.

279
00:17:50,890 --> 00:17:52,170
It's not fair.

280
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:57,760
You know I can't refuse 
when you tell me that.

281
00:17:58,030 --> 00:17:59,070
I'm sorry.

282
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:02,470
We're unfair, but please forgive us.

283
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:04,640
Emilia...

284
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:08,120
No! I'm staying! I want to stay with you!

285
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:13,470
Please! Please! I don't... 
I don't want to be alone!

286
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:17,150
You will never be alone.

287
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:22,900
I will always be right there with you.

288
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:27,710
In the memories that come forth 
when you close your eyes...

289
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:31,980
In dreams, where you hug 
yourself and feel warm...

290
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:36,240
In the echoes you hear when 
you shout into the sky...

291
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:40,110
I will always be with you.

292
00:18:40,470 --> 00:18:43,200
I'm with you forever and ever.

293
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,420
You're lying... You're lying!

294
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:48,070
You're a liar, Mother!

295
00:18:49,930 --> 00:18:51,940
Emilia, I promise.

296
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:07,540
You and I will always be together.

297
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:11,180
I'll promise you that right now.

298
00:19:12,450 --> 00:19:16,090
Really? You'll stay with me?

299
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,680
Yes, really.

300
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,960
More than anyone, Emilia...

301
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:26,860
Lia... I love you more than 
anyone else in this world.

302
00:19:36,250 --> 00:19:38,160
Mother Fortuna...

303
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:41,740
I love you too, Mother.

304
00:19:42,210 --> 00:19:43,740
I love you!

305
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:48,930
I love you... I love you, Mother Fortuna.

306
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:54,460
I love you so much... so much... so much!

307
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,620
Lia, I love you.

308
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:05,380
I love you, Emilia.

309
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:10,130
Why? Why did this happen?

310
00:20:10,130 --> 00:20:12,650
Because I broke my promise and left my room?

311
00:20:12,650 --> 00:20:14,900
No! It's not your fault at all!

312
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:16,610
It's no one's fault!

313
00:20:16,610 --> 00:20:20,180
They why? Why do we have to leave?

314
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:23,600
Should I have stayed locked 
up in my room forever?

315
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:26,880
Then no one would leave, 
and everyone could stay together?

316
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:27,780
You're wrong, Emilia!

317
00:20:28,210 --> 00:20:30,140
Was I bad?

318
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:33,290
Is that why everyone hates me,
 and I end up alone?

319
00:20:33,290 --> 00:20:35,830
No! That's not true, Emilia!

320
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:38,100
No one hates you!

321
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:41,460
Everything in this world 
exists to bless you!

322
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,350
Th-The Black Serpent?

323
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:58,110
The crucible of disease... 
The plague-bearing mabeast?

324
00:21:00,190 --> 00:21:01,230
Fula!

325
00:21:02,180 --> 00:21:03,520
Huma!

326
00:21:04,450 --> 00:21:05,390
Archi?

327
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:08,160
It's nothing. I'm fine.

328
00:21:08,970 --> 00:21:11,160
Everything is... fine.

329
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:25,190
Emilia... See the white flowers 
between those two trees?

330
00:21:25,190 --> 00:21:25,870
Uh-huh.

331
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,590
Can you run toward those flowers?

332
00:21:29,170 --> 00:21:33,090
Run through them, and keep running straight.

333
00:21:33,770 --> 00:21:36,720
I can... I can run.

334
00:21:37,370 --> 00:21:38,070
But...

335
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:42,320
Don't worry, Emilia. You won't be alone.

336
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,530
Archi...

337
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:47,730
Now, run!

338
00:21:47,730 --> 00:21:49,660
Don't look back, no matter what you hear!

339
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:54,630
Yes, that's right.

340
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:56,870
Just keep running.

341
00:21:57,330 --> 00:22:00,070
Just like the way you always 
give us the run-around.

342
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:08,100
You think I'm going to let you go?

343
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,720
Fortuna-sama...

344
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:15,710
I know your daughter will be just fine.

345
00:22:25,530 --> 00:22:28,050
Even after... all this...

346
00:22:28,450 --> 00:22:32,580
Look, why don't you just 
admit that it's hopeless?

347
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:42,660
In the end, that's all there was to 
your resolve, your determination, and all that.

348
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:46,080
It's not like I'm doing 
this because I'm a sadist.

349
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:49,910
It just looks like I'm tormenting 
you because you're weak.

350
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:55,550
Do not criticize him too harshly,
 Bishop Corneas.

351
00:22:55,970 --> 00:22:59,940
You are more special and perfect than anyone,
 and that makes you wonderful...

352
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:04,020
And they are also wonderful 
in their imperfection.

353
00:23:05,430 --> 00:23:09,200
You just keep giving me more work 
to do, you incompetent fool.

354
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:10,910
Al Fula!

355
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:15,280
Hang on, Geuse!

356
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:18,930
Fortuna-sama... Is Emilia-sama—

357
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:21,250
I sent her out of the forest with Archi,

358
00:23:21,250 --> 00:23:22,520
thanks to you.

359
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:26,090
That is... good to hear...

360
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:29,800
There's nothing good about it!

361
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:34,400
Who the hell do you think 
you are, coming back here?

362
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:38,140
I was about to crush his head under my foot!

363
00:23:38,370 --> 00:23:39,600
Me!

364
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:42,900
What gives you the right, 
who gave you permission,

365
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:48,440
to interfere with me, me, me, me, me?!

366
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,790
Wait, Bishop Corneas.

367
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:52,530
Huh? What was that, Pandora-sama?

368
00:23:52,740 --> 00:23:54,880
Calm your anger.

369
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:58,320
I will not allow you to kill them here.

370
00:23:58,320 --> 00:24:01,710
Do you feel nothing when 
you see the two of them?

371
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:11,260
Did you just order me to calm my anger?

372
00:24:12,010 --> 00:24:16,350
Don't get cocky with that 
unassuming attitude, woman!

373
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:23,020
No...

374
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:27,660
That's what happens when 
you mouth off to me.

375
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:30,080
Don't interfere with me!

376
00:24:30,470 --> 00:24:32,490
Don't interrupt when I'm talking!

377
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:36,380
Fortuna-sama, please run—

378
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:38,180
Don't be a fool.

379
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:40,370
I left Emilia to come back here.

380
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:42,740
But why would you...

381
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:44,540
To keep you from dying.

382
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,930
And so that if you did die,

383
00:24:48,830 --> 00:24:50,780
I'd be by your side.

384
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:55,340
If you were no longer in this world,

385
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,950
if you stopped coming to this forest,

386
00:24:58,370 --> 00:25:00,460
what would I have to wait for?

387
00:25:01,330 --> 00:25:06,880
I couldn't endure such a long 
time without you. I'm too weak.

388
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:09,320
You... are not weak.

389
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:10,820
I am!

390
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:16,200
I was only acting tough in 
front of you and Emilia.

391
00:25:21,180 --> 00:25:21,870
Tch!

392
00:25:22,130 --> 00:25:28,090
You wanna ignore me that long and 
then have fun on your own? Fine!

393
00:25:28,090 --> 00:25:30,960
I'll crush you both into 
nothing but a pool of blood!

394
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:34,840
I told you to wait, Bishop Corneas.

395
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:44,540
I will forgive all of your violent 
actions and rash outbursts.

396
00:25:45,030 --> 00:25:48,720
My goal in bringing you here 
has already been fulfilled.

397
00:25:49,370 --> 00:25:51,920
You are free to leave now.

398
00:25:52,610 --> 00:25:56,100
You brought me here, but now you're 
satisfied, so you're telling me to leave?!

399
00:25:56,100 --> 00:25:57,820
What kind of fool do you think I—

400
00:25:57,820 --> 00:26:00,980
I see. Then I will take it upon myself.

401
00:26:01,750 --> 00:26:05,290
Bishop Corneas should not be here.

402
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:09,200
He is in his own mansion, 
surrounded by his wives.

403
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:09,540
Wai—

404
00:26:13,440 --> 00:26:16,790
I've sent the noisy young man away.

405
00:26:17,690 --> 00:26:20,850
Now we can talk at leisure.

406
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:24,430
Can I ask one thing first?

407
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:28,140
Didn't you get blown to 
pieces and die earlier?

408
00:26:28,480 --> 00:26:29,310
I'm sorry?

409
00:26:29,950 --> 00:26:32,400
Perhaps your eyes deceived you?

410
00:26:33,170 --> 00:26:35,840
Now that Bishop Corneas is gone,

411
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:39,470
naturally, the results of 
his actions are gone, too.

412
00:26:39,470 --> 00:26:41,120
Th-This is...

413
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:46,030
But I will not rewrite your being 
overtaken by the Sloth Witch Factor.

414
00:26:46,030 --> 00:26:49,170
I wish to commend you on your behavior,

415
00:26:49,170 --> 00:26:53,460
and the behavior of this 
woman who came back for you.

416
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:01,140
Fortuna-sama!

417
00:27:01,990 --> 00:27:04,760
Let us defeat her together!

418
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:08,580
Right now, we must do what 
we can for Emilia-sama!

419
00:27:13,120 --> 00:27:15,530
Freeze the fluctuation 
of time itself to white,

420
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:21,030
Demon Ice of antiquity that brings 
eternal sleep to the soul!

421
00:27:22,580 --> 00:27:27,010
My life, my mission, all of my deep love...

422
00:27:27,010 --> 00:27:29,460
Here and now, for this very moment!

423
00:27:30,670 --> 00:27:33,290
Now, come.

424
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:38,630
Hold me to you and let me feel 
the extent of your resolve.

425
00:27:38,630 --> 00:27:41,630
The Day Betelgeuse Laughed

426
00:27:44,590 --> 00:27:46,200
Mother Fortuna...

427
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,770
Geuse... Archi...

428
00:27:48,210 --> 00:27:52,020
I have to... I have to do something, too.

429
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:54,610
Bring the key and seal here.

430
00:27:58,670 --> 00:28:00,070
Seal?

431
00:28:02,740 --> 00:28:04,850
If that's that you want,

432
00:28:05,380 --> 00:28:08,140
I'll just give it to you.

433
00:28:08,610 --> 00:28:09,860
It's where that thing is...

434
00:28:10,690 --> 00:28:11,580
But...

435
00:28:31,910 --> 00:28:33,640
The fairies?

436
00:28:34,020 --> 00:28:36,650
Are you showing me?

437
00:28:37,100 --> 00:28:40,220
The seal... is that way?

438
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:44,140
I can save Mother and everyone else?

439
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:07,650
I want to be with you all again!

440
00:29:07,650 --> 00:29:10,510
I'll be a good girl!

441
00:29:20,910 --> 00:29:22,280
Welcome.

442
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:28,160
I've been waiting for you.

443
00:29:28,160 --> 00:29:38,160


